course: dictionary
lesson: 5566
title: Leprosy: a word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Leprosy is an illness caused by tiny germs called bacteria. They harm the skin and nerves, so a person can lose feeling in their hands and feet. Today it can be cured with medicine, and it is hard to catch.
explain: In the Bible, leprosy meant several skin diseases, and people with it had to live apart from others. «Jesus touched people with leprosy, whom others avoided.» Touching them showed that he cared for people others pushed away.
explain: Context helps you work out the meaning. «Jesus healed ten men with leprosy» tells you people can be healed from it, which fits the science meaning. Check by swapping in your meaning: "Jesus healed ten men with an illness caused by germs" still makes sense.
fact: Leprosy is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «leprosy», not «a leprosy».
fact: «Leprosy» means an illness caused by germs (bacteria) that harms the skin and nerves.
fact: In the Bible, «leprosy» meant several skin diseases, and people with it had to live apart from others.
fact: Today leprosy can be cured with medicine, and it is hard to catch.
fact: Useful phrases: «suffer from leprosy», «cure leprosy», and «leprosy mission».
exercise: «Jesus touched people with leprosy, whom others avoided.» What is leprosy? | A kind of stone found in caves | *An illness caused by germs that harms the skin and nerves | A feeling of being very happy | A type of bread eaten at weddings
exercise: Leprosy harms the nerves. What can a person lose because of it? | *Feeling in their hands and feet | Their voice | Their birthday | Their shadow
exercise: Today, leprosy can be ___ with medicine. | counted | copied | cooked | *cured
test: In the Bible, people with leprosy had to do what? | Sail across the sea | Wear gold crowns | Sing in the temple choir | *Live apart from other people
test: «Jesus healed ten men with leprosy, but only one came back to say thank you.» What did that one man do that the others did not? | *Came back to say thank you | Ran away from the town | Wrote a book about it | Asked for money
exam: Which sentence best describes what Jesus did for people with leprosy? | He sent them into the desert to live alone | He ignored them completely | *He touched them and healed them when others avoided them | He wrote them letters and went away
